Cloud models are the Foundation of accessibility of cloud resources. 

Public cloud
Public cloud is accessible to all users. It is owned by a third party cloud provider that offers cloud services to customers at a cost.
In this model users pay for what they consume in a pay-as-you-go model.

Private cloud
Private cloud is owned by a single entity and is only accessible to users from that single entity. It is used for compliance and regulatory measures.
In this model users pay for the security, infrastructure and maintainance. Which costs more than paying for what you consume.
This offers the most control over the underlying hardware. 

Hybrid cloud.
Hybrid cloud is a combination fo both private and public cloud. Commonly used for cloud bursting.
In this case, the private cloud could be used for sensitive data, while public cloud is used for Analytics. 
